<p>All Rum is made from fermenting and then distilling sugar cane molasses or sugar cane juice, but White Rum has an ageing process that makes the liquor clear.</p>
<p>Rum is usually aged, and the container it’s aged in has a big say in its colour.</p>
<p>In bourbon or other wooden casks, the rum turns a dark brown colour, but in stainless steel tanks it stays colourless. Rum that’s been aged in wood can also be filtered to take the colour out.</p>
<p><em><strong>White Rum is clear because it’s aged in stainless steel, or filtered after ageing.</strong></em></p>
<p>Pretty cool, huh?</p>
